# Changelog

Do not append to `changelog.md` and do not run `bun run bump` on a pull request.

- A release runs `bun run bump release`. That fills an empty `## Unreleased` from merged pull request titles, then promotes it.
- `bun run bump next --publish` publishes a prerelease and does not touch the changelog.
- Groups, when a release writes them: `### ✨ Added`, `### 💥 Breaking Changes`, `### ♻️ Changed`, `### ⚠️ Deprecated`, `### 🔥 Removed`, `### 🐛 Fixed`, `### 🔒 Security`.
- A breaking title uses `type(scope)!: summary` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` line in the commit body.
- Never append under a shipped `## vX.Y.Z` section.
